<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $13.1 mln Feb 27.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $13.1 mln Feb 27.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $13.1 million deficit on Feb 27 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 27</p>
<p>Exports: $254.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $190.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $226.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $304.1 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $13.1 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.131 million</p>
<p>Imports: $3.098 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.507 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.619 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $921 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
